  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759126,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 100 Classic Book Collection: Synopsis\n\nTransform your Nintendo DS into a portable library with *100 Classic Book Collection*, a unique e-book collection developed by Genius Sonority and published by Nintendo. This innovative game, also known as *100 Classic Books* in North America, houses a remarkable selection of one hundred public domain literary works, including titles by William Shakespeare, Charles Dickens, and Gaston Leroux.\n\nExperience classic literature in a novel way by holding your DS like a book and utilizing the touch screen to turn pages. Customize your reading experience with adjustable text sizes, background music, and a convenient bookmark feature. Discover new authors and genres with the in-game search function, and even take a personality quiz to receive personalized reading recommendations. \n\nOriginally released in Europe in December 2008, with subsequent releases in Australia and North America, this game offers a unique blend of entertainment and education. While the availability of free downloadable books ended in 2014, the core collection remains a compelling way to engage with timeless literature on the go."
    },
